## 0. R2 was NOT reachable — say it first

Every farm issue points its repro at `s3://zenfuzz/crashes/rav1d-safe/<target>/<arch>/<sig>/`
with a `/mnt/v/fuzzes/_farm/...` mirror. **Neither is reachable from this machine**, so the
farm's own artifacts were not obtained for ANY of the 22 issues:

  * `~/.config/cloudflare/` does not exist (no `r2-credentials`, no `cf-token-mint`)
  * `~/.aws/` does not exist; no `R2_*` / `AWS_*` in the environment; nothing in
    `~/.zshrc`, `~/.zshenv`, `~/.zprofile`, `~/.profile`; `security find-generic-password
    -s R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID` finds no keychain item
  * `/mnt` does not exist on this macOS box, so the `/mnt/v/fuzzes` mirror is absent
  * no public R2 domain: `https://zenfuzz.r2.imazen.org/...` and
    `https://fuzz.r2.imazen.org/...` both return curl code `000` (DNS failure) on the
    repro, metadata and prefix keys
  * the issue bodies carry no inline repro — `grep -lis base64 issue_*.txt` over all 22
    bodies matches nothing

`aws` and `s5cmd` are installed; there is simply no credential to give them. Triage below
therefore rests on in-repo repros, on the `__ablate` liveness counters, on git archaeology
of the reported panic locations, and on re-fuzzing this tree — not on the farm artifacts.


