### 1a. Planted-panic proof (the harness fails when the decoder panics)

A `panic!` was planted at the top of all seven aarch64 MC dispatchers, on the BPC16 branch
only, and reverted afterwards. The harness went red and named every pair:

    24 regression seed/entry-point pairs PANICKED — a previously-fixed crash is back: [
      "tests/crash_vectors/arm_mc16_avg_overshoot.obu (raw) via decode_obu:
         PLANTED avg 16bpc dispatcher reached",
      ... (4 entry points x 6 seeds)
    ]
    test result: FAILED. 2 passed; 1 failed

That run doubles as the **MC liveness map** the activity counters cannot provide (there is
no `ablate::note()` site in `mc_arm.rs`). Each committed seed reaches exactly the dispatcher
it was filed against:

    arm_mc16_avg_overshoot.obu       -> avg 16bpc          (guards #442)
    arm_mc16_mask_overshoot.obu      -> mask 16bpc         (guards #438)
    arm_mc16_blend_dir_overshoot.obu -> blend_dir 16bpc    (guards #443)
    arm_mc16_w_mask_overshoot.obu    -> w_mask 16bpc       (guards #441)
    arm_mc16_overshoot.obu           -> mc_put 16bpc       (guards #430/#436/#439/#444)
    arm_mc16_blend_overshoot.obu     -> mc_put 16bpc first

The last row is why a second, isolated run was needed: with only the `blend` panic planted,
`arm_mc16_blend_overshoot.obu` reaches `blend_dispatch_inner` 16bpc and is the only seed
that does (guards #440). Six of six seeds, six of six dispatchers, individually proven.

