## 2. Re-fuzzing this tree found a LIVE bug that is not any of the 22

600 s of `cargo +nightly fuzz run parse_seq_header` on aarch64, seeded with the whole
regression corpus and `fuzz/av1.dict` (19 611 execs, 1 966 new units, peak RSS 673 MB):

    src/owned_recon.rs:367:37: range end index 128 out of range for slice of length 64

`cargo fuzz tmin` -> **21 bytes**. It reproduces through the plain stable harness on all
four entry points, at `threads = 1`, so it is not a tile-threading-only path. A separate
600 s `decode_obu` run found the same signature independently from a different input
(89 bytes) — the same cross-target duplication the farm's own issue set shows.

Backtrace: `splat_dc` (ipred.rs:552) -> `for_rows_mut` (owned_recon.rs:512) -> `px_mut`.

Root cause, measured with a temporary instrument at the overrun site rather than inferred:

    OOB-DIAG for_rows_mut: bytes.len=8192 px_size=2 stride_bytes=64 pxstride=32
                           base_off_px=2048 row=63/64 off_px=4064 w=64 h=64
                           need_end_bytes=8256

The band is 32 pixels wide; the intra DC block is 64. `band_geometry` sized the column
extent as exactly the tile's live width while the ROW extent has always been a full
`sb_step * 4` with live rows clamped separately. AV1 codes whole blocks and crops on
output, so a block may legally overhang the tile's last column; the picture absorbs that in
its padding, a column-compact band has none. Only the LAST row panics — rows 0..h-2 land in
the NEXT band row, which is live and gets stitched back to the picture: **silently wrong
pixels**, not just a crash. 8bpc is mostly shielded by accident (the 64-byte CHUNK rounding
is 64 pixels of slack at one byte per pixel, 32 at two).

Fixed on this branch: the allocation rounds up to a whole superblock, `live` still records
the exact `cols`, so `stitch` copies what it always did.

    before fix: fuzz_regression FAILED, 4 pairs panicked
    after fix:  fuzz_regression ok, 3 passed
    decode_md5_verify t=1: TOTAL: 766 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped
    decode_md5_verify t=8: TOTAL: 766 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped (RAV1D_MD5_THREADS=8)

The widening is live on that corpus, not dead code — instrumented, it fires with
`cols=352 -> alloc_cols=384` (luma, 128px superblocks) and `176 -> 192` on both chroma
planes, and md5 stays 766 with it firing.

Not verified: no valid-stream repro is committed. Producing one needs an encoder that emits
a >=10-bit frame narrower than its superblock; the fuzz seed is the gate.


